From: ESP32-S3 IoT Finder <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: refresh Time Advertisement on each beacon

hostapd builds the 802.11v Time Advertisement element once and caches it,
even though the comment in hostapd_update_time_adv() notes that the Time
Value should be calculated from the current TSF.  After the first beacon the
advertised UTC is therefore stale by the time hostapd has been running.

Refresh the element on every call where it is emitted.  This keeps the
direct-UTC interpretation used by OpenWrt/hostapd up to date.  It is a
workaround for AP-side time distribution, not a change to the 802.11 frame
format.

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_shared.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_shared.c
@@ -651,8 +651,7 @@ u8 * hostapd_eid_time_adv(struct hostapd_data *hapd, u8 *eid)
 	if (hapd->conf->time_advertisement != 2)
 		return eid;
 
-	if (hapd->time_adv == NULL &&
-	    hostapd_update_time_adv(hapd) < 0)
+	if (hostapd_update_time_adv(hapd) < 0)
 		return eid;
 
 	if (hapd->time_adv == NULL)
